design:
The tool input should be `{ kind, name? , ref?, systemId? }`; omitted `systemId` means use the campaign binding. Tool data should include `{ record, sourcePack, license, overrideChain }`. Prompt language should say before running any creature or rules mechanic, call `lookup_rules`; avoid D&D-only wording such as SRD or monster/spell/class only.

Initial test sketch:
```ts
const registry = createDefaultToolRegistry();
expect(registry.list()).toContain('lookup_rules');
expect(buildSystemPrompt(registry)).toContain('lookup_rules');
const result = registry.invoke('lookup_rules', { kind: 'creature', name: 'Goblin' }, ctx());
expect(result.ok).toBe(true);
```
